{
  "description": "Signal-detection-theory engine — noise and signal+noise evidence distributions (unit-variance Gaussians separated by dPrime) are plotted on a math-canvas; the learner drags the decision criterion and the theoretical hit rate Φ(d′ − c) and false-alarm rate Φ(−c) recompute (the ROC point), and RUN_TRIALS samples empirical hits and false alarms at the configured base rate. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
